"""MCP6042T-I/MS - Microchip dual 600 nA/channel rail-to-rail I/O op amp, MSOP-8.

Primitive package (bare device). MCP6042 is the dual member of the MCP6041/2/3/4
family (DS20001669E): 14 kHz GBWP, 0.6 uA typ quiescent current per amplifier,
unity-gain stable, rail-to-rail input (VSS-0.3 V to VDD+0.3 V) and output.
Supply VDD-VSS = 1.4 V to 6.0 V (Table 1-1 note 1: date codes from Nov 2007 are
screened to 6.0 V). Industrial grade -I: -40 to +85 C specified.
T = tape and reel ordering suffix; /MS = 8-lead MSOP (drawing C04-111C).

Pinout (MSOP-8, datasheet p.1): 1 OUTA, 2 VINA-, 3 VINA+, 4 VSS, 5 VINB+,
6 VINB-, 7 VOUTB, 8 VDD.

Integrator-owned: the local VDD bypass capacitor (datasheet section 4.6:
0.01 uF to 0.1 uF within 2 mm of VDD; bulk >= 1 uF within 100 mm optional and
shareable), the feedback/gain network, and any output isolation resistor for
capacitive loads (section 4.2, Figure 4-4). Tie unused channels as a follower
to a mid-rail or rail voltage within the common-mode range. With ~pA input
bias currents, PCB leakage dominates high-impedance nodes; consider guard rings
(section 4.7).

SPICE: Microchip MCP6041 macro model Rev D (MCP6041_MM_D.zip, covers
MCP6041/2/3/4) wrapped as a dual subcircuit. It models typical linear-region
behaviour; set GMIN=100f for high-impedance circuits.
"""

load("@stdlib/interfaces.zen", "Opamp")

VDD = io(Power(voltage="1.4V to 6.0V"))
VSS = io(Ground)
A = io(Opamp)
B = io(Opamp)

Component(
    name="MCP6042T-I_MS",
    symbol=Symbol(library="MCP6042T-I_MS.kicad_sym"),
    pins={
        "OUTA": A.OUT,
        "-INA": A.IN_N,
        "+INA": A.IN_P,
        "VSS": VSS,
        "+INB": B.IN_P,
        "-INB": B.IN_N,
        "OUTB": B.OUT,
        "VDD": VDD,
    },
    spice_model=SpiceModel(
        "MCP6042.lib",
        "MCP6042",
        nets=[A.OUT, A.IN_N, A.IN_P, VSS, B.IN_P, B.IN_N, B.OUT, VDD],
        args={},
    ),
)
